From c6862f9c031fb273c81d284ab5c4cef9f83e2067 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AFOT Bot <afot@example.com>
Date: Sun, 12 Jul 2026 04:56:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] fix(rust): propagate errors instead of unwrap-panicking
 (20+ call sites)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Every public OverdriveDb method did:

    let lib = ffi::load();
    let func: Symbol<...> = lib.get(b"overdrive_xxx").unwrap();

across open, open_with_options, sync, close, version, create_table,
drop_table, list_tables, table_exists, insert, get, update, delete,
count, query, search, begin/commit/abort_transaction, verify_integrity —
32 total .unwrap() calls in rust/src/. A stale or mismatched native
binary turned every DB call into a hard, unrecoverable panic.

Switches every call site to ffi::try_sym(...)? / ffi::try_to_cstr(...)?
and propagates via Result. version() now returns Result<String> instead
of String (was calling .unwrap() internally with no way to report
failure). Drop::drop() no longer panics on symbol-resolution failure
either — a panic during an already-unwinding Drop aborts the process,
so it now just best-effort no-ops on failure instead.

Also documents (no behavior change) that insert_batch() is not atomic:
it loops calling insert() per document, so a failure partway through
leaves prior documents committed with no rollback.

Verified end-to-end against the real bundled liboverdrive.so:
  version: Ok("2.3.0")
  inserted id: users_1
  doc: {"_id":"users_1","name":"Karthikeyan","role":"founder"}
  count: 1

Depends-on: fceed3a (fix(rust): stop panicking on native symbol/library resolution)
